            "text": "DOM-based XSS (innerHTML sinks, XML/AJAX sources) — Requires further review: https://testphp.vulnweb.com/AJAX/index.php (innerHTML sinks) + AJAX/infoartist.php|infocateg.php|infotitle.php|showxml.php\n\nTarget unreachable. Static review of the archived AJAX/index.php (retrieved from Wayback) shows DOM XSS sinks: SetContent()/SetInfo() build HTML strings from XML node values and assign to `document.getElementById('contentDiv').innerHTML` / `infoDiv.innerHTML`, and xmlCompleted() does `xd.innerHTML = httpreq.responseText` from POST showxml.php. Inputs are DB/XML-derived (AJAX/infoartist.php|infocateg.php|infotitle.php) rather than directly attacker-controlled, so exploitability depends on whether an unauthenticated user can write into those DB fields — could not be tested live. Gap: no live DOM/DB-write test."
